				<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite.toml</code> for
				everything that tunes how Aphrodite compresses, and Hermes's own
				<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">config.yaml</code> for
				enabling the plugin.
			</p>

			<div class="grunge shell-card mt-8 p-5 sm:p-8" data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">
				<CodeFence Lang="toml" Code={Config} />
				<div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 border-t border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)] pt-3 text-base text-zinc-dust">
					<span>TEMPLATES IN THE REPO:</span>
					<span class="font-bold text-stamped-canary">
						aphrodite.toml.example + the embedded template
					</span>
				</div>
				<div class="prose-flow mt-2 max-w-[46rem]">
					<p class="type-body text-zinc-dust">
						Two shipped files stay in sync: aphrodite.toml.example (the annotated
						reference) and the embedded template the binary ships with.
					</p>
					<p class="type-body text-zinc-dust">
						Keys not yet wired into the runtime are annotated DOCUMENTED BUT UNWIRED in
						the example - it is the source of truth for the documented surface.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
					<div class="well p-4">
						<ZineKicker Tone="teal" As="div">
							TWO PARSERS, ONE FILE
						</ZineKicker>
						<p class="mt-2 type-body text-bone-newsprint">
							The Rust HTTP proxy (
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								config/proxy.rs
							</code>
							) reads{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[[proxies]]</code>
							,<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[defaults]</code>
							, the four hot-reload thresholds plus auto_expand / auto_expand_limit /
							max_request_body_size, and preview_max_chars. The Hermes dylib session (
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								config_loader.rs
							</code>
							) reads the{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								[compression]
							</code>
							engine keys,{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[defaults]</code>
							model/api_url,{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[flow]</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								[directives]
							</code>
							,<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[prompts]</code>{" "}
							and
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">[templates]</code>
							.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="well p-4">
						<ZineKicker Tone="teal" As="div">
							NOT HERMES'S CONFIG.YAML
						</ZineKicker>
						<p class="mt-2 type-body text-bone-newsprint">
							The only Aphrodite-relevant keys in
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								config.yaml
							</code>{" "}
							are
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								plugins.enabled: [aphrodite]
							</code>
							, added by{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								hermes plugins enable
							</code>
							, and optionally{" "}
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
								context.engine: aphrodite
							</code>
							with its threshold. Ports, thresholds, preview style and prompt wording
							all belong in the toml.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-8 type-body text-zinc-dust">
					Every knob the file exposes is explorable on
					<a
						class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
						href={Routes.Config}
					>
						/config/
					</a>
					, and the complete schema is
					<a
						class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
						href={DocsRoute("config/aphrodite-toml")}
					>
						/docs/config/aphrodite-toml/
					</a>
					.
				</p>
			</div>
			<ZineSource
				Lines={[
					"SRC: aphrodite.toml.example (the annotated reference)",
					"SRC: docs/config/aphrodite-toml.md; docs/config/env-vars.md",
				]}
			/>
		</section>

		<!-- 06 // VERIFICATION - the six ways an install announces its own failure -->
		<section class="blueprint-section relative w-full" data-reveal>
			<p class="section-index">06 // VERIFICATION // FAILURES // WHAT THE MESSAGE MEANS</p>
			<h2 id="failures" class="mt-3 type-section text-bone-white">
				When it does not come up
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-[46rem] type-body text-bone-newsprint">
				Every install failure announces itself in one of six ways. The proxy's own stderr
				goes to
				<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
					~/.hermes/aphrodite/proxy-stderr.log
				</code>
				- read that file before anything else.
			</p>

			<div class="grunge shell-card mt-8" data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">
				<div class="overflow-x-auto">
					<table class="w-full border-collapse font-mono text-base">
						<thead>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-well-edge)] text-left">
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									SYMPTOM
								</th>
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									CAUSE
								</th>
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									FIX
								</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody class="text-bone-newsprint">
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									the plugin logs the setup command and stays disabled
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									binaries missing from ~/.hermes/aphrodite/binaries/
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									bash download.sh (or pwsh ./download.ps1) in the plugin folder
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									download.sh stops at the verify step
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									checksum does not match SHA256SUMS.txt
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									re-run the script; check network access to GitHub Releases
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									no API key configured
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									no aphrodite.toml in the working directory
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">--api-key or APHRODITE_API_KEY</td>
							</tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									port already in use
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									another proxy already bound to 9797/9798
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									tail proxy-stderr.log; APHRODITE_CACHE_PORT /
									APHRODITE_TOKEN_PORT
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									the binary is SIGKILLed on launch (macOS)
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									quarantine, or no Xcode Command Line Tools
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									re-run aphrodite setup - ditto, xattr -c, ad-hoc codesign
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">
									a health-poll warning after launch
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-zinc-dust sm:px-5">
									a port did not answer within 5 seconds
								</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									the warning names the port; check proxy-stderr.log
								</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p class="mt-8 max-w-[46rem] type-body text-zinc-dust">
				Before launching, the plugin probes both ports' /health endpoints and skips the
				launch when another process already answers a confirmed Aphrodite health body - so a
				second Hermes session does not start a second proxy pair. A failed registration is a
				warning, never an abort.
			</p>
			<ZineSource
				Lines={[
					"SRC: docs/install/troubleshooting.md (checklist, in order)",
					"SRC: docs/install/index.md (which artifact do you need)",
				]}
			/>
		</section>

		<!-- 07 // STANDALONE - the same engine without Hermes, and the cheapest
		     proof that the binary itself serves. -->
		<section class="blueprint-section relative w-full" data-reveal>
			<p class="section-index">07 // PROXY // THE STANDALONE LANE</p>
			<h2 id="proxy" class="mt-3 type-section text-bone-white">
				Run it without Hermes
			</h2>
			<div class="prose-flow mt-6 max-w-[46rem]">
				<p class="type-body text-bone-newsprint">
					The same compression engine runs as a standalone proxy: point any
					OpenAI-compatible client's
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">base_url</code> at
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
						http://localhost:9798
					</code>
					(token) or <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">:9797</code>
					(cache), and responses compress over plain HTTP.
				</p>
				<p class="type-body text-bone-newsprint">
					Invoked without an
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite.toml</code>, the
					binary needs{" "}
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">--api-key</code> or
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">APHRODITE_API_KEY</code>.
					That is a startup requirement, not an upstream call - a placeholder is enough to
					prove the binary serves.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="grunge shell-card mt-8 p-5 sm:p-8" data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">
				<div class="overflow-x-auto">
					<table class="w-full border-collapse font-mono text-base">
						<thead>
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-well-edge)] text-left">
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									PORT
								</th>
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									MODE
								</th>
								<th class="type-meta px-4 py-3 font-black uppercase text-stamped-canary sm:px-5">
									WHAT IT SERVES
								</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody class="text-bone-newsprint">
							<tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)]">
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">9797</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-weathered-teal sm:px-5">cache</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									the cache proxy - threshold 2048 bytes by default
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-bone-white sm:px-5">9798</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 text-weathered-teal sm:px-5">token</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
									the token proxy - threshold 256 bytes by default
								</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>

				<p class="mt-8 font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
					START // the binary, no Hermes
				</p>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mt-3"
					Copy
					Code={`./aphrodite --api-key «redacted:sk-...» --listen 127.0.0.1:9798`}
				/>
				<p class="mt-2 type-body text-zinc-dust">
					The key is redacted here on purpose: a placeholder is enough, because the flag
					is a startup requirement rather than a credential the binary verifies.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-6 font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
					CHECK // the health endpoint
				</p>
				<CodeFence Class="mt-3" Copy Code={`curl http://127.0.0.1:9798/health`} />
				<p class="mt-3 font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal">
					EXPECT // the health body
				</p>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mt-3"
					Lang="json"
					Code={`{"status":"healthy","ccr":true,"mode":"token","version":"<current version>","fill_pct":...}`}
				/>
				<div class="mt-6">
					<ZineReveal
						Cover="aphrodite: no API key configured - set APHRODITE_API_KEY env var or api_key in aphrodite.toml"
						Tag="STDERR"
						Raw={`<span class="text-stamped-canary">No aphrodite.toml in the working directory</span> - the CLI mode has no config to read a key from, so the flag (or the env var) is the whole requirement.`}
					/>
				</div>
				<div class="prose-flow mt-6 max-w-[46rem]">
					<p class="type-body text-zinc-dust">
						You do not need a real Hermes session, a real Hermes install or a real
						upstream API key to confirm the binary itself works: starting the proxy and
						hitting
						<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">/health</code> never
						calls upstream. Set
						<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
							APHRODITE_NO_AUTO_LAUNCH=1
						</code>
						if you launch it yourself and do not want the plugin to start a second pair
						- there is no{" "}
						<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">auto_start</code> key
						in either config file.
					</p>
					<p class="type-body text-zinc-dust">
						The full surface is documented on the proxy pages:
						<a
							class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
							href={DocsRoute("proxy/architecture")}
						>
							architecture
						</a>
						,
						<a
							class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
							href={DocsRoute("proxy/compression")}
						>
							compression
						</a>
						,
						<a
							class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
							href={DocsRoute("proxy/handlers")}
						>
							handlers
						</a>
						,
						<a
							class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white"
							href={DocsRoute("proxy/retry")}
						>
							retry
						</a>
						.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<ZineSource
				Lines={[
					"SRC: docs/install/troubleshooting.md (verify the proxy without Hermes)",
					"SRC: docs/proxy/architecture.md; docs/proxy/compression.md",
				]}
			/>
		</section>

		<!-- 08 // UNINSTALL - the reverse direction, as two complete lanes -->
		<section class="blueprint-section relative w-full" data-reveal>
			<p class="section-index">08 // UNINSTALL // THREE COMMANDS AND A DIRECTORY</p>
			<h2 id="uninstall" class="mt-3 type-section text-bone-white">
				Uninstall
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-[46rem] type-body text-bone-newsprint">
				Disable the plugin, remove the loader, then stop anything still running. Every
				command is its own copy control, so a reader never pastes the sentence about the
				command.
			</p>

			<div class="grunge shell-card mt-8 p-5 sm:p-8" data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
					{Uninstall.map((Lane) => (
						<div class="well p-4">
							<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
								<span class="telemetry-tag telemetry-tag--teal">
									{Lane.Shell.toUpperCase()} - {Lane.Platform}
								</span>
							</div>
							<ol class="mt-3 list-none">
								{Lane.Steps.map((Step, Index) => (
									<li class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-[color:var(--tier-well-edge)] pl-3">
										<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
											<span class="font-mono text-base font-black tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
												{String(Index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
											</span>
											<span class="font-mono text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white">
												{Step.Title}
											</span>
										</div>
										<div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
											<code class="type-code break-token text-bone-newsprint">
												{Step.Command}
											</code>
											<ZineCopyChip
												Label="COPY"
												Copy={Step.Command}
												Aria={`Copy the command: ${Step.Command}`}
												Color="teal"
											/>
										</div>
									</li>
								))}
							</ol>
						</div>
					))}
				</div>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-[46rem] type-body text-bone-newsprint">
					Remove{" "}
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
						~/.hermes/aphrodite/
					</code>{" "}
					as well to clean up the binaries, config, CCR database and logs the download
					scripts or{" "}
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite setup</code>{" "}
					wrote.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2 max-w-[46rem] type-body text-zinc-dust">
					On Windows the runtime home is
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">
						%USERPROFILE%\.hermes\aphrodite\
					</code>
					.
				</p>
			</div>
			<ZineSource
				Lines={[
					"SRC: docs/install/macos-linux.md (uninstall); docs/install/windows.md (uninstall)",
				]}
			/>
		</section>

		<!-- THE NATURAL NEIGHBORS -->
